Base dtor
The destructor is statically bound, so ~Base() is invoked rather than ~Derived(). This is problematic: even though
Derived itself is not managing dynamic memory, its member variable items is. Since the destructor for Derived was
not called, the members introduced by Derived were also not destructed. Running Valgrind on the program illustrates
the issue:
