assert(node_ptr);
// check whether this is a past-the-end iterator
Iterator tmp = *this;
// make a copy of this iterator
node_ptr = node_ptr->next;
return tmp;
// return the copy
}
We need not provide a parameter name, since we are not actually using the parameter object. In keeping with the contract for postfix increment,
the function returns a copy of the original iterator by value.
